# Test hints for SessionScopedCart
mode: interpreter
# Driving this example means being the same caller twice: log in, add to the
# cart, then read the cart back and see the item. The integration harness uses
# HTTP::Tiny, which only keeps cookies when HTTP::CookieJar is installed — and
# without them every request is a fresh caller, so an empty cart and a broken
# feature look identical. The executor picks the jar up automatically when the
# module is present (AROTest::Executor::HTTP); until it is, the scoping itself
# is covered by CallerScopedStorageTests and SessionServiceTests.
skip: needs HTTP::CookieJar to be the same caller across two requests
skip-on-windows: HTTP server tests not supported on Windows CI
